          {
            "text": "The answer is `{\"invariant_exists\": false}`, now written to the output file. I got this by reading the code, not by running the tests, and I didn't open the test file itself.\n\n`offset == 0` does not hold every time line 1206 runs:\n\n- **How `offset` changes:** It is set to 0 once, at line 1188, before the `while` loop. Line 1206 (`offset += end - start`) then adds the length of each tag it finds, and nothing resets it between loop passes.\n- **Why that breaks the property:** `offset` is 0 only the first time line 1206 runs in a call. If a string has two or more tags, `offset` is already positive (the length of the first tag) when line 1206 runs again.\n- **Which tests do that:** Going by the class names, the multiple-embedded, adjacent-vars, repeated-var and four-tags tests all pass strings with more than one tag. So some runs of that line see a nonzero `offset`.\n\nThe Google Drive connector couldn't be used here because it needs authorization first. You can authorize it in your claude.ai connector settings; this task didn't need it.",
